cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "contract-review-eval-harness"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Förste"
    given-names: "Sebastian"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastianfoerste/contract-review-eval-harness"
license: MIT
version: 0.7.0rc1
date-released: 2026-09-03
abstract: >-
  A deterministic, offline harness that scores AI contract reviews against
  hand-written answer sets for synthetic contracts. It measures clause
  extraction, risk-flag precision, recall and severity, and citation
  grounding, where every citation must be an exact span of the normalised
  contract. A release policy turns the scores into a decision (PILOT_ELIGIBLE,
  HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED or REJECT) recorded in a release certificate. No LLM
  grades the reviews.
keywords:
  - legal AI
  - contract review
  - evaluation
  - benchmark
  - citation grounding
  - hallucination
  - release gate
